


Variable
==============
Variable is name of storage location where we can store data

Java support 3 type of variable
----------------------------------
1.Local variable
------------------------
If any variable created inside any function/block or constructor is called
local variable

Scope: Within a method
Memory allocation: At the time of method execution
Memory deallocation: After method execution

2.Instance variable
------------------------
If any variable created inside class and outside any method/block is called
instance variable

Scope: Within a Object
Memory allocation: At the time of Object creation
Memory deallocation: After Object execution

Note:
For every new Object instance variable will get new memory 

3.Static variable
------------------------
If any variable created inside class  with static keyword and outside any method/block is called
static variable

Scope: Within a Class
Memory allocation: At the time of class Loading
Memory deallocation: After class unload

Note:
Static variable creates one time memory and share that with all objects

======================================================
Type of Methods
------------------
1.Instance method
2.Static Method

1.Instance method
============================
-Any method design without static keyword is an Instance method
-Instance method always we can call through Object
-Instance method get new memory once new object created


2.Static Method
======================
-Any method design with static keyword is called static method
-Static method get called through ClassName so object is not required
-Static method will get only one time memory and shared with all object




















